// RA4 fixture (the RA3 fixture's) (as the RA2 fixture's): the global rules of the small two sided world of the RA1 fixture, with values of
// production, selling and repair that differ from the shipped ones, so that the tests of RA2
// read them from here: a unit queue holds one item and 3 behind it; a sale refunds 40 percent;
// a repair step restores 10 hit points every 5 ticks (a vehicle on a depot every 4) for 20
// percent of the price over a whole repair. Fixture data (invariant I10); the values of the
// groups later milestones consume are placeholders within their ranges.
//
// RA5 fixture: with the ore and the crates of RA5. A map amount of 25 is a bail of ore and of 50
// a bail of gems, at most 12 bails a cell; every 40 ticks every cell of ore below 12 bails grows
// and every cell above 6 bails spreads (both certain: the tests that need a chance edit the
// permille); at most 3 crates, one at the start, a taken one replaced after 50 to 200 ticks,
// with every content at a share of its own and three unit types.
(
    schema_version: 2,
    production: (
        build_ticks_per_1000: 840,
        multiple_factory_pm: 800,
        wall_build_time_pm: 3000,
        low_power_penalty_pm: 1000,
        min_low_power_speed_pm: 500,
        max_low_power_speed_pm: 800,
